hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1462","Muhammad bin Amr bin Tammam Al-Masry told us, Nu’aym bin Hammad told us, Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Sa’ib said: I attended the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the day of Eid. He prayed and said: “We have completed the prayer, so whoever wishes may sit.” For the engagement, and whoever wants to go goes.” Abu Bakr said: This is a strange Khorasani hadith. We do not know of anyone who narrated it except Al-Fadl bin Musa Al-Shaybani. This news was also with my father. Ammar, on the authority of Al-Fadl bin Musa, he did not narrate it to us in Nishapur, the people of Baghdad narrated it, as some Iraqis told me."
